{
  "title": "Plantar Fibromatosis (Ledderhose Disease)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8061/plantar-fibromatosis-ledderhose-disease",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Nov 19 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Plantar Fibromatosis, also known as Ledderhose disease, is a benign tumor of the foot plantar fascia that is characterized by myofibroblast and collagen proliferation.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The condition usually presents in elderly patients with subcutaneous thickening or nodules in the foot.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with a combination of physical examination and MRI studies.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is observation for minimally symptomatic lesions. Surgical excision is recommended for lesions that are large, painful, or activity-limiting.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common soft tissue neoplasm in the foot",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "more common in **males**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "usually seen in **middle-aged or elderly individuals**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "can affect individuals of all ages",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**bilateral in 25-50%**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "male gender",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Caucasian",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "epilepsy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "repeated trauma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "diabetes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "long-term alcohol use",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "chronic liver disease",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "other fibrosing conditions (see below)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "occurs in 3 phases",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**proliferative phase**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "characterized by increased fibroblast activity and cell proliferation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**involutional/active phase**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "characterized by nodule formation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**residual/resting phase**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "characterized by decreased fibroblast activity, collagen maturation, and scar/contracture formation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "unlike Dupuytren's disease, the genetic basis of plantar fibromatosis is unclear",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Dupuytren's disease**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "occurs in 25% with Dupuytren's",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**Peyronie's disease**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Plantar fascia",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8061/images/orr-11-001fig1.jpg",
              "caption": "anatomy"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**comprised of 3 bands**: central, medial, lateral",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**medial band most commonly affected**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "originates from the medial and anterior aspects of the calcaneus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "divides into 5 digital slips at the MTP joints",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "inserts on the base of the proximal phalanges",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually asymptomatic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may become painful",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**subcutaneous thickening or nodules**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8061/images/3a.jpg",
                      "caption": "bilateral"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "usually on medial aspect of plantar foot",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**digital contractures**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "rare",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "evaluate for the presence of other fibrosing conditions (Dupuytren's, Peyronie's)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "document ankle and hindfoot motion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "evaluate for the presense of Achilles tendon or gastrocnemius contractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lateral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "usually normal",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "imaging study of choice",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "nodular thickenings on the **medial aspect** of the plantar aponeurosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**low signal intensity on T1-weighted images**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8061/images/11a.jpg",
                          "caption": "T1 MRI"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "due to the relative acellularity and high collagen content of lesions",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**low or medium signal intensity on T2-weighted images**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8061/images/12a.jpg",
                          "caption": "T2 MRI"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "can have areas of high signal intensity if aggressive type",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ultrasound",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "multiple lesions embedded on the plantar fascia with sharp juxtaposition between the less reflective fibroma and the much brighter plantar fascia surrounding it",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**comb sign**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8061/images/65b07b1a97d956ee166777e050f408_big_gallery..jpg",
                      "caption": "ultrasound comb sign"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "alternating linear bands of hypoechogenicity and isoechogenicity relative to the plantar fascia",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "represents the hyperechoic, fibrous regions of the fibroma on a background of hypoechogenic cellular matrix",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Histology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "gross anatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "lobulated firm irregular mass",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "histology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8061/images/fibromatosisplantartypemicro2.jpg",
                  "caption": "Histology"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "dense fibrocellular tissue with mature collagen and fibrocytes in various stages of maturation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "no atypical features or abnormal mitotic activity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Post-traumatic neuroma",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Fibrosarcoma",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Clear cell sarcoma",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "observation and supportive therapy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first line of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "lesions that are small or minimally painful",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "modalities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "NSAIDs",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "orthotics",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "physical therapy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "corticosteroid injections",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "radiotherapy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "excision +/- radiation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "lesions that are large, painful, or activity-limiting",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Excision +/- Radiation**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**total fasciectomy is preferred over local or wide excision due to risk of recurrence**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "57-100% recurrence with local excision",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "8-80% recurence with wide excision (2-3cm margins)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "0-50% recurrence with total fasciectomy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "avoid incisions directly over nodules",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "may lead to local recurrence due to intimate association of the nodule and skin",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "if performing a partial fasciectomy, it is important to resect the nodule and the overlying skin",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "may require skin grafting",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "complications specific to this treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "skin necrosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "nerve entrapment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "loss of arch height",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "outcomes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**high rate of local recurrence with high-grade lesion**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "consider postoperative radiation to minimize recurrence",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Recurrence**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "incidence",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "occurs in 60% of excised lesions",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**usually recurs as a more aggressive lesion**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "risk factors",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "bilateral disease",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "multiple nodules",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "family history of plantar fibromatosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "prevention",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "can perform adjuvant radiation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
